          "summary": "Chief Economic Adviser V Anantha Nageswaran said foreign capital is returning sharply, helped by oil falling below $100 a barrel and worries over AI stock valuations elsewhere. He said earlier pressure on the rupee from AI-related outflows could turn into strength. Business Standard separately reports FPIs have bought over ₹88,000 crore of Indian shares this month, the fastest pace since November 2020.",
